.TH SSLTEST 1
.SH NAME
ssltest \- test an ssl(3) cipher end to end
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ssltest
[
.I alg
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Ssltest
drives a cipher of the
.IR ssl (3)
device (\c
.BR "#D" )
the way
.IR crypt (1)
does \(em an ssl conversation over a pipe, used as a filter \(em to
check that it seals and opens correctly. It defaults to
.BR chacha20_poly1305 ,
the AEAD (RFC 8439) record protection this tree added for encrypted
.IR import (4)/9export (1);
another
.I alg
(e.g.\&
.BR "rc4_256 sha1" )
can be given.
.PP
It seals a message under a 32-byte key and checks that:
.IP \(bu
the ciphertext differs from the plaintext (encryption happened);
.IP \(bu
opening it with the same key recovers the original plaintext;
.IP \(bu
a ciphertext with one bit flipped is
.I rejected,
not opened \(em the authentication tag catches it;
.IP \(bu
a wrong key does not recover the plaintext.
.PP
The last two are automated negative controls: for an AEAD, silently
decrypting tampered or wrong-key input to garbage-or-plaintext is the
failure that would look like success.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/ssltest.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR ssl (3),
.IR crypt (1),
.IR import (4)
.SH BUGS
Tests one cipher over a local pipe; it does not exercise a real
.IR import (4)
mount between two hosts. Harmless
.B fdtochan
diagnostics from the kernel appear as each pipe reaches end of file.
